<p>If the printer is equipped with the document server inside, document 
 data can be stored in the document server for printing.</p>
<p>The document server stores documents data for later printing. The data 
 can be combined and finishing such as stapling and punching can be specified 
 when printing. Even document data from different computers or document 
 data scanned from a scanner can be combined.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>You can optionally set user ID, file name, password, 
 and user name for each file depending on your purpose.</p></li>
<li><p>Depending on the printer you are using, custom 
 paper size document files cannot be stored in the document server.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Setup</span> menu 
 of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Type:</span> 
 list, select <span class="Term-Soft">Document Server</span> and click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Job 
 Type Details</span> dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Click the <span class="Term-Soft">&lt;&lt; Collapse list</span> button if the <span class="Term-Soft">Job 
 Type:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> 
 tab is not displayed.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">User ID:</span> list, 
 select a user ID type.<br/>
 If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Create Own ID</span>, enter a user 
 ID in the <span class="Term-Soft">Enter User ID:</span> box using up to 
 eight characters, which are alphanumeric (a-z, A-Z, and 0-9) characters 
 and symbols ('_', '.', '-', '/', and ':').<br/>
 If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Windows Login Name</span>, the 
 user ID may appear as the following:</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">If the number 
 of characters in your Windows login name exceeds 20 single-byte characters, 
 your user ID will only display up to 20 single-byte characters.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="5">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">File Name:</span> 
 box, enter a file name using up to 16 characters except double quotation 
 marks (optional).</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Password:</span> 
 box, enter a 4 to 8 digits password (optional).<br/>
 If a password is used for a file, it must be entered on the printer's 
 control panel for editing or printing the file stored in the document 
 server.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="7">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">User Name:</span> 
 box, enter a user name using up to 16 characters except double quotation 
 marks (optional).</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Folder Number:</span> 
 box, enter the number for the folder where you store the document data. 
 If you specify "0", the document will be stored in the <span class="Term-Hard">Shared Folder</span>.<br/>
 If the folder is password-protected, enter the password in the <span class="Term-Soft">Folder Password:</span> box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">When saving 
 document data in the document server, there are some settings unavailable 
 and those cannot be selected. If you want to change settings such as finishing, 
 specify the settings when printing the document from the document server.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="11">
<li><p>Start the print job.<br/>
 The document is stored in the document server.</p></li>
</ol>
